MiOS Hypr3D Retina window opening (applies after hypr3d-mios-frame-rate.patch). Operator 2026-10-23: "default
Hypr3D window opening distance/size should be Zoom/Scale/DPI/Resolution/Formatting(Landscape, Portrait, Mobile,
etc-etc) aware ... launch to Retina specifications based on text-size". A window that enters the room (the 3D
toggle, or a window mapping while the room is open) opens at magnification M = 1 (its on-screen size / its 2D
size): one snapshot texel per output pixel at the window centre and across it (no minification blur), and every
client's glyphs at their flat-desktop size, whatever font, app zoom or text scaling the client renders with. For a
camera-facing window M = window_scale x d1 / distance, d1 = (logical height / 100 / 2) / tan(kFovDeg / 2) -- the
1:1 distance the fullscreen passthrough and the view morph already use -- so the stock 0.5 / 5 m gave M = 0.85 on
1080p, 1.13 on 1440p and 0.66 on a 390x844 phone (measured). Every key defaults to upstream behaviour; mios-gen
(tools/native/mios-gen/src/hypr3d_spawn.rs, [desktop.hyprland.hypr3d.spawn]) sends them at the room toggle (toggle_key, SUPER+F12):

- windows.pixel_exact: window_scale = spawn_distance / d1(target monitor), re-derived every frame from the
  plugin's own monitor size (follows mode, scale and transform changes and hot-plug). The reading distance stays a
  world constant, so the enter/exit morph and the fullscreen passthrough become a pure dolly at constant text size.
- windows.fit ("off" | "resize" | "distance") and windows.fit_margin (logical px): the work area (the monitor minus
  its reserved bars) shrunk by the margin. "resize": a window larger than it gets a room box that fits (the morph
  drives the real client box, the client re-renders at 1:1; the spawn box of a window mapping in the room is
  clamped the same way); a client that keeps a larger box (min or fixed size) is pushed back about the eye until
  it fits -- never cropped. "distance": push back only. Fresh windows centre on the work area (where the 2D
  `center` rule puts them) whenever fit is on.
- windows.pixel_snap: once a fresh window's snapshot box holds still, a sub-pixel shift lands its texel grid on
  the output pixel grid (at render.scale 1 a half-pixel phase washes 1-px detail out completely).
- windows.cascade (logical px): a window opening over another steps right/down in the plane instead of 0.15 m
  toward the eye (M 1.031); any depth step toward the eye (stacking, dialogs 0.3 m in front of their parent) is
  compensated by a per-window scale multiplier kept with the saved pose, so M stays 1.
- windows.min_magnification: the push-back legibility floor (status flag "small").
- render.texel_sharp: at 1:1 and magnified, each window texel is flat over the scene pixels it covers and only the
  pixel a texel edge crosses blends, so with render.scale >= 1.5 a 1:1 window keeps 1-px detail at full contrast
  (bilinear then the SSAA box halves it: modulation 0.5). Minified textures keep the mip + anisotropic path; the
  pane, rim and edge pass are untouched (one glass look).
- static_assert: mios-gen mirrors kFovDeg = 65 and LOGICAL_PX_PER_UNIT = 100; the build fails when upstream changes
  either.
- The status file gains "spawn: exact= scale= d= d1= M= fit= area= snap= cascade= sharp= spawnBox= placed=
  resized= pushed= snapped= last= box= lastM= dist= mul= k= dx= dy= small=".

Frame rate, captures and stills are unaffected: placement runs once per window (no pass, no capture), and a fitted
box never takes the tiled capture path.

